cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Julia Time, please cite it as below."
title: "Julia Time: a local, single-player game for learning Julia through data and probability"
abstract: >-
  A locally-run browser game in which the player types real Julia and the screen answers.
  Six connected steps, each a practice lesson and then a chapter of one case (The Case of
  the Missing Fleas, a simulated springtail mystery), cover data handling, grouping,
  joining tables, sampling, simulation, and careful interpretation. Optional extras let
  the player work on their own CSV file (typed CSV.read, lm and an optional Poisson glm)
  and time six calculations in Julia, R and Python in a speed lab.
type: software
